sanctioned: this program reads a two-store inner join on sqlite::memory: through `Store.select` and `Store.selectToList` / `Store.selectToMaybe` in every call form whose projection is visible through the call spine. Ipe.Db.Store is an Ipê-only addition with no counterpart in the reference backend, and Ipê emits Rust+sqlx while the reference emits a different backend, so a shared Main.ipe cannot run on both. Ipê's output is recorded as the correct reference. The output lines assert, in order, that each form reads the projected rows and never the placeholder `Err`: (1) the direct call; (2) the direct call as a helper argument inside a list literal; (3) `j |> Store.select f |> Store.selectToList db` over a two-column tuple; (4) `j |> Store.select f |> Store.selectToMaybe db` over a join matching exactly one pair; (5) `Store.selectToList db <| Store.select f j`; (6) `(Store.select f >> Store.selectToList db) j`; (7) `Store.selectToList db (j |> Store.select f)`; (8) a let-bound join piped through both. List lines are sorted, since an inner join without an ordering fixes no row order.
